.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Unicode Wizard

@Contents
$^#Unicode Wizard (version 1.6 from 26.01.2006)#

    This plugin, Unicode Wizard (UWizard), is intended for "#editing#" and
"#viewing#" of files in #unicode#, #utf-7#, #utf-8# and #quoted-printable# encodings.
For #base64# it is possible only to decode and only in the ~editor~@Editor@.

    UWizard allows working with those files as if they where archives. Upon
entering such an "archive" you will see a file with the original contents, but
it will already be decoded to OEM (in the case of quoted-printable, the
decoded file can be in any other codepage, such as koi8-r, that depends on the
program that created the file and not on UWizard). Changes made to that file
will be reflected on the original file.

    Files encoded in Unicode and UTF-8 are automatically recognized by the
plugin, if they have the appropriate signatures, upon "Enter" in panels. If
such signatures are not found but you are sure that you know the encoding of
the file, you can run UWizard manually from the command line.

    And even more, UWizard can work with files already opened in the editor.
For that you should run it from the editor, simple eh?

    ~Working in editor~@Editor@
    ~Working in panels~@PanelsMenu@
    ~Command line~@CMD@
    ~About the author...~@author@

