@CMD
$^#Command line syntax#


    To open the plugin from the command line, user menu or file associations
you can use the commands below:

  #UWA#:#FileName#
  #UW#:#FileName#
  #UBE#:#FileName#
  #UTF7#:#FileName#
  #UTF8#:#FileName#
  #QP#:#FileName#

  #UWA#, #UW#, #UBE#, #UTF7#, #UTF8#, #QP#
    Plugin's prefixes (in accordance to autodetection, #Unicode#, #Unicode Big Endian#,
#UTF-7#, #UTF-8# and #Quoted-printable#)

  #FileName# - the name of the file you want to process.


    To automatically decode and open a file in the internal viewer without
opening plugin's panel, use the following commands:

  UWA:#<#FileName
  UW:#<#FileName
  UBE:#<#FileName
  UTF7:#<#FileName
  UTF8:#<#FileName
  QP:#<#FileName


    To automatically decode and open a file in the internal editor without
opening plugin's panel, use the following commands:

  UW:#*#FileName
  UW:#*#FileName
  UBE:#*#FileName
  UTF7:#*#FileName
  UTF8:#*#FileName
  QP:#*#FileName

    If the file opened in such way is changed then all the changes will be
reflected on the original file.

    If you feel uncomfortable using the command line, you can always open the
plugin through the standard F11 ~menu~@PanelsMenu@.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
@Editor
$^#Unicode Wizard: working in editor#

    The plugin can encode the contents of the file being edited from the
currently selected codepage to UTF-7, UTF-8 or quoted-printable and to decode the file
contents from Unicode, UTF-8, quoted-printable or Base64 encodings to the
codepage selected in the editor. Working with UTF-7, UTF-8 and Unicode is available
only when the current editor's codepage is OEM (when you see DOS in the status
line).

    #Always process only selected area#
    If this option is on then the plugin will always process only the selected
area. If this option is off then the plugin will process the selected area if
such exists or the whole file if there is no selection. When processing the
whole file (only when there is no selection!) and decoding from
quoted-printable then occurs concatenation of lines ending with '='.

    #Translate result to the current editor's codepage#
    The work order in editor: the data is decoded from the current codepage
(usually selected by #F8# or #Shift-F8#) to OEM, then the selected action
from the menu is preformed (encoding or decoding of the data according to the
selected item), after all this, if the option "#Translate result to...#" is
on, then the data will also be translated from OEM to the current codepage.

    #Notes#
    Encoding to Unicode is not available because of the internal workings of
FAR editor - in which the data is processed line by line, because of that the
plugin can only encode to Unicode each line separately, after saving such a
file you will get anything but only not a correct file in the Unicode
encoding. If it is a necessity for you to be able to edit unicode files then
run the plugin from the ~command line~@CMD@, and there you will come to the
particulars.
    If when decoding from Base64 you have some other not Base64 encoded text in
the file you must select and operate with the Base64 encoded section only.
    When decoding from Base64 the line is always processed as a whole,
even if only part of the line is selected, because of the specifics of
this encoding.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
@PanelsMenu
$^#Unicode Wizard: working in panels#

    The menu command is applied to the file currently under cursor.

    #Panel: Autodetect#
    UWizard detects Unicode and UTF-8-files by checking for standard sequences
of bytes in the beginning of the file (FEFF, FFFE and EFBBBF, also see
uwizard.ini description). If such
sequence is not found then autodetection ends without success. If the file
type was detected then a standard UWizard panel is created and opened, if the
file type was not detected then no panel is created.

    #Panel: Unicode, Unicode Big Endian,#
    #UTF-7, UTF-8, Quoted-printable#
    It is considered that the file under cursor is Unicode, Unicode Big Endian, UTF-7, UTF-8 or
Quoted-printable accordingly, the corresponding panel is then created and
opened.

    #Editor: Autodetect#
    When the file type is detected successfully (see above) that file is then
translated to OEM and the result is opened in a modal editor. If the file
opened in the editor in such a way is changed then after closing the editor
all the changes will be applied to the original file. If autodetection wasn't
successful then simply the file under cursor is opened in a regular non modal
editor.

    #Editor: Unicode, Unicode Big Endian,#
    #UTF-7, UTF-8, Quoted-printable#
    It is considered that the file under cursor is Unicode, Unicode Big Endian, UTF-7, UTF-8 or
Quoted-printable accordingly.

    #Viewer: Autodetect#
    When the file type is detected successfully (see above) that file is then
translated to OEM and the result is opened in the viewer. If autodetection
wasn't successful then the original file is opened in the viewer.

    #Viewer: Unicode, Unicode Big Endian,#
    #UTF-7, UTF-8, Quoted-printable#
    It is considered that the file under cursor is Unicode, Unicode Big Endian, UTF-7, UTF-8 or
Quoted-printable accordingly.


 ~Contents~@Contents@
